{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792935274,"nonce":"TqzVNgHdmxD9Oae3CEoe7Lg7ybg=","title":"cbproj: Haxe class paths and defines","message":"Part of 5ed625d51a511b21c35b0b711cf6ddb898831a2fa7bccabc1ecf3bb1973d123a (the project format RayDE opens).\n\nA project's Haxe code may live outside it. RayDE's own build.hxml uses\n../ashui/haxe and four more. Today a `.cbproj` passes only its source roots\nas `-cp`, and includes every module in them, because another language may\nimport any of them.\n\n```toml\n[haxe]\nclass-paths = [\"../ashui/haxe\", \"lib\"]   # relative to the project file\ndefines = { chimpmonk_editor = true, ash_version = \"2\" }\n```\n\n- **Keys.** They are rayzor.toml's `[build]` keys, so RayDE's cards carry\n  over.\n- **What is compiled.** The source roots stay included whole. The extra class\n  paths are `-cp` only, compiled as far as the program reaches.\n- **Defines.** `true` is a bare `-D name`; any other value is\n  `-D name=value`.\n- **Libraries.** Haxelibs stay in `[dependencies.haxe]`.\n- **Validation.** An unknown key in `[haxe]` is an error that names the\n  key. A missing class path is an error naming the path.","files":null}]}